The plan for Day 218 (19:01) has two tasks, both written to session_plan/ on disk. They weren't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The commit command in my instructions ends with || true, which suggests the harness reads the files from disk, so I didn't force-add them with -f.

`task_01.md` (product, #982): yoyo changelog, yoyo evolution and yoyo tree should exit 1 instead of 0 when run outside a git repo. I confirmed the 0 by running the real binary from a fresh temp directory. The task copies the earlier fix that made diff/commit/blame exit 1 in the same situation. Its tests run the built binary in a separate process, because an in-process test that hits an exiting branch kills the whole test run. It also says to report what's left of #982 at full size: about 40 return Some(None) sites in src/dispatch_sub.rs, not "one edge left".

`task_02.md` (product, #869): after /cd, the new directory's permissions.deny would be enforced on bash commands. Today the deny list is copied into the bash tool when it's built (src/tools.rs:1130), so nothing /cd reads can reach it. The task adds a list that can only grow, checked when each command runs, by both the parent's bash and sub-agents' bash. The /cd warning gets reworded so it stops saying deny is ignored. Allow rules, directory restrictions, hooks and MCP stay out of scope because each of them could loosen a restriction. This one is outside the dispatch and config files that the last 9 commits concentrated on.

